# Walkthrough - WBCSD Protocol Upgrade

I have completely upgraded the application to ensure compliance with the **WBCSD Cement Industry Protocol**. The system now supports comprehensive Scope 1 (Process & Energy) and Scope 2 (Electricity) calculations with automatic formula application.

## 1. Backend Upgrades

### Models ([emissions/models.py](file:///c:/Users/samsung/Desktop/cement/backend/emissions/models.py))
- **FuelConsumption**: Added `biomass_percentage` to separate biogenic (neutral) from fossil emissions.
- **ClinkerProduction**: Added `non_carbonate_mgo_contribution` to refine calcination emission factors.
- **ElectricityConsumption (NEW)**: Added support for Scope 2 location-based reporting.
- **RawMaterialConsumption (NEW)**: Added Method B (Input-based) for calcination when clinker data is unavailable.

### Calculation Engine ([emissions/signals.py](file:///c:/Users/samsung/Desktop/cement/backend/emissions/signals.py))
Implemented automatic calculation logic triggered on every save:
- **Combustion**: $Energy \times EF \times (1 - Biomass\%)$
- **Calcination (Method A)**: $Clinker \times [0.785(CaO\% - CaO_{nc}) + 1.092(MgO\% - MgO_{nc})]$
- **Calcination (Method B)**: $Material \times Carbonate\% \times 0.44 \times (1 - Moisture\%)$
- **Electricity**: $kWh \times GridEF$

## 2. Frontend Upgrades

### Protocol Calculator ([components/emissions/ProtocolCalculator.tsx](file:///c:/Users/samsung/Desktop/cement/frontend/src/components/emissions/ProtocolCalculator.tsx))
A new, comprehensive calculator wizard that guides the user through calculation steps:
- **Scope 1 Process**: Toggle between Method A (Output/Clinker) and Method B (Input/Raw Material).
- **Scope 1 Energy**: Enhanced fuel input with biomass deduction.
- **Scope 2**: Electricity consumption input.

### Emission List ([components/emissions/EmissionList.tsx](file:///c:/Users/samsung/Desktop/cement/frontend/src/components/emissions/EmissionList.tsx))
Updated to display all four categories of emission data:
- Clinker Production
- Raw Material Consumption
- Fuel Consumption (with Fossil vs Biogenic split)
- Electricity Consumption

## User Action Required
**Database Migration**: Since new models and fields were added, you must run the following commands in the backend terminal:
```bash
python manage.py makemigrations
python manage.py migrate
```
Then restart the backend server.
